	(text "K-12 / DECIDED 29 Sep: Rev B 48 V stage is an LM51551 flyback (plain boost hits the 93 % duty limit).\nTopology follows TI SNVSB75E Figure 10-12 'Typical Non-Isolated Flyback'; BIAS tied to VCC for 1S start (>=2.97 V).\nDesign calculations: docs/handover/FLYBACK_DESIGN.md (fsw ~300 kHz, n = Ns/Np = 5, Lp ~7 uH, Ipk ~3.1 A at 3.0 V / 100 mA).\nT301 = Coilcraft HPH6-0090L: pri 3-10, sec = 5 windings in series. Leakage is NOT published: clamp and snubber values need bench tuning.\nCompensation values are PRELIMINARY (depend on T301 and the PMD401 cable/bulk capacitance) - simulate/bench before use.\nKill path: UVLO/EN driven by FLY_EN (sheet 'Kill path'). EN < 0.4 V min (SNVSB75E) = shutdown. A flyback has no DC path\nfrom VBAT to the output, so EN low de-energises the rail. ECO1 (owner approved architecture): no output switch; rail control is EN; R312 bleeder and D303 clamp fitted.\nE-06: every 48 V capacitor rated >= 100 V. E-03: 45.6-50.4 V at the PMD401."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 20 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "e9d30e74-a3c9-56a9-bd05-b69c2cef901e")
	)
